<article class="env-lemma" id="048R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/048R">Lemma <span data-tag="048R">83.5.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme, and let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to B$ be a geometric point of $B$. Let $j : R \to U \times _ B U$ be a pre-equivalence relation over $B$. In this case the weak orbit of $\overline{u} \in U(k)$ is simply </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{  \overline{u}' \in U(k) \text{ such that } \exists \overline{r} \in R(k), \  s(\overline{r}) = \overline{u}, \  t(\overline{r}) = \overline{u}' \}   \]
</div>
  <p> and the orbit of $\overline{u} \in U(k)$ is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{  \overline{u}' \in U(k) : \exists \text{ field extension }K/k, \  \exists \  r \in R(K), \  s(r) = \overline{u}, \  t(r) = \overline{u}'\}   \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because by definition of a pre-equivalence relation the image $j(R(k)) \subset U(k) \times U(k)$ is an equivalence relation. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>